{"name":"Spirit","hex":"#b2bbc6","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Spirit","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Ellipsis of Holy Spirit."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Spirit"}],"entries":[{"title":"Liquor","blocks":[{"text":"Liquor, spirit, distilled spirit, or spirituous liquor are alcoholic drinks produced by the distillation of grains, fruits, vegetables, or sugar that have already gone through alcoholic fermentation. While the word liquor usually refers to distilled alcoholic spirits instead of drinks produced by fermentation alone, it can sometimes be used more broadly to refer to any alcoholic beverage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Liquor_Still_Frankfort_489226997.jpg/330px-Liquor_Still_Frankfort_489226997.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liquor","wikidata":"Q56139"},{"title":"Spirit (animating force)","blocks":[{"text":"In religion and philosophy, spirit is the vital principle or animating essence within humans or, in some views, all living things. Although views of spirit vary between different belief systems, when spirit is contrasted with the soul, the former is often seen as a basic natural force, principle or substance, whereas the latter is used to describe the organized structure of an individual being's consciousness, in humans to include their personality. Spirit as a substance may also be contrasted with matter, where it is usually seen as more subtle, an idea put forth for example in the Principia Mathematica."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spirit_(animating_force)","wikidata":"Q120312205"},{"title":"Spirit (Spirit album)","blocks":[{"text":"Spirit is the debut studio album by American rock band Spirit, released on January 22, 1968 by Ode Records. The album was commercially successful, spending more than six months on the Billboard album charts, peaking at No. 31. It was voted number 658 in Colin Larkin's All Time Top 1000 Albums 3rd Edition (2000)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c7/Spiritfirstalbum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spirit_(Spirit_album)","wikidata":"Q1136326"},{"title":"Spirit (rover)","blocks":[{"text":"Spirit, also known as MER-A or MER-2, is a Mars robotic rover, active from 2004 to 2010. Spirit was operational on Mars for 2208 sols or 3.3 Martian years. It was one of two rovers of NASA's Mars Exploration Rover Mission managed by the Jet Propulsion Laboratory (JPL). Spirit landed successfully within the impact crater Gusev on Mars at 04:35 Ground UTC on January 4, 2004, three weeks before its twin, Opportunity (MER-B), which landed on the other side of the planet. Its name was chosen through a NASA-sponsored student essay competition. The rover got stuck in a \"sand trap\" in late 2009 at an angle that hampered recharging of its batteries; its last communication with Earth was on March 22, 2010."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/KSC-03PD-0786.jpg/330px-KSC-03PD-0786.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spirit_(rover)","wikidata":"Q176276"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Spirituosen-im-supermarkt.jpg/500px-Spirituosen-im-supermarkt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Spirituosen-im-supermarkt.jpg/1280px-Spirituosen-im-supermarkt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Spirituosen-im-supermarkt.jpg/500px-Spirituosen-im-supermarkt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A display of various liquors in a REWE supermarket in Brandenburg, Germany","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASpirituosen-im-supermarkt.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/17-05-06-Miniaturen_RR79033.jpg/500px-17-05-06-Miniaturen_RR79033.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/17-05-06-Miniaturen_RR79033.jpg/1280px-17-05-06-Miniaturen_RR79033.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/17-05-06-Miniaturen_RR79033.jpg/500px-17-05-06-Miniaturen_RR79033.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Some single-drink liquor bottles available in Germany","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A17-05-06-Miniaturen_RR79033.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Viru_Valge_1L.jpg/500px-Viru_Valge_1L.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Viru_Valge_1L.jpg/500px-Viru_Valge_1L.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Viru Valge, an Estonian vodka","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AViru_Valge_1L.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Brewing_and_distillation_industries._%28_1858-_%29.jpg/500px-Brewing_and_distillation_industries._%28_1858-_%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Brewing_and_distillation_industries._%28_1858-_%29.jpg/500px-Brewing_and_distillation_industries._%28_1858-_%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An illustration of brewing and distilling industry methods in England, 1858","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrewing_and_distillation_